## Protect your kidneys

- take your blood pressure medicines, and check your blood pressure if advised
- eat less **salt**
- stop smoking, and keep alcohol within recommended limits
- stay a healthy weight and keep active

## Medicines

Tell every doctor, dentist and pharmacist that you have CKD. Avoid anti-inflammatory painkillers such as ibuprofen unless your doctor says they are safe. Some medicines are paused if you are ill and dehydrated. Ask your team about **sick day rules**.

## Diet

Most people with mild CKD just need a healthy, balanced diet. If your CKD is more advanced, a **kidney dietitian** may advise on **potassium**, **phosphate** or fluid. Do not restrict these without advice.

## Vaccines

Have the **flu**, **COVID-19** and **pneumonia** vaccines.

## Support

**Kidney Care UK** offers advice, counselling and grants, and **Kidney Research UK** has information.
